<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  English strings: the whole app's user-facing copy, in one catalogue.

  It lives in core:designsystem because every feature module already depends on
  it, and a single catalogue is what keeps shared copy (errors, actions, units)
  from being duplicated and drifting across seven feature modules.

  Every user-facing string in the app lives in a resource file; nothing is
  hardcoded in Kotlin. The Telugu translation in values-te/ carries the same
  keys, so a missing translation is a visible gap rather than a crash.

  Anything describing an estimate says so explicitly. That wording is a product
  requirement, not a stylistic choice: the app must never let a person mistake
  a geometric estimate for a measurement.
-->
